{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Terms of use — extdir{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}Terms of use for extdir, a free non-commercial directory.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
        <h1>Terms of use</h1>
        <p>Nutzungsbedingungen. Short, because the service is free and sells nothing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
        <h2>What this is</h2>
        <p>
            extdir is a free, non-commercial directory of open-source Shopware 6 extensions. There is
            no account, no payment, no contract and nothing on sale. You may use it, link to it and
            quote from it.
        </p>

        <h2>What the data means</h2>
        <p>
            Compatibility information is derived from the version constraints maintainers declare in
            their own <code>composer.json</code>. It records what they <em>said</em>, not what has been
            tested. No extension listed here has been installed or verified against a running Shopware
            instance by extdir.
        </p>
        <p>
            Licence information is detected automatically from package metadata. It is a strong
            indication, not legal advice, and it is not a substitute for reading the licence yourself
            before shipping someone else's code in production.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
            The directory is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. The data may be incomplete,
            out of date or wrong. Installing third-party extensions in a production shop is your
            decision and your risk. To the extent permitted by law, the operator accepts no liability
            for damages arising from use of this site or of any software it describes, except in cases
            of intent or gross negligence, or where liability is mandatory by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Ranking</h2>
        <p>
            Placement is determined by a published algorithm and nothing else. There are no paid
            placements, no featured slots, no sponsorships and no manual boosting.
            <a href="{{ path('ranking') }}">The formula is public</a>, and the code that implements it
            is in the public repository.
        </p>

        <h2>Automated access</h2>
        <p>
            Crawling for research or interoperability is fine if it is reasonable — a few requests per
            second, an identifying user agent, and respect for <code>robots.txt</code>. Do not scrape
            aggressively enough to degrade the service for other people.
        </p>

        <h2>Content that is not ours</h2>
        <p>
            Extension names, descriptions and trademarks belong to their respective owners. Each
            indexed extension is governed by its own licence. Nothing here grants you rights to
            third-party software beyond what that software's licence already gives you.
        </p>

        <h2>Removal</h2>
        <p>
            Maintainers can have their extension corrected or removed at any time under the
            <a href="{{ path('takedown') }}">takedown policy</a>, without giving a reason.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
            German law applies. If any provision here is invalid, the rest remains in force.
        </p>

        <p class="small subtle page-note">
            Last updated: {{ 'now'|date('Y-m-d') }} ·
            <a href="{{ path('imprint') }}">Imprint</a> ·
            <a href="{{ path('privacy') }}">Privacy</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
